  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of archived Alaska Medicaid Human Chorionic Gonadotropin (HCG) criteria; metadata effective date 2019-01-15 retained. PDF Version 1 was last updated and approved 5/3/2011.",
    "Reimbursible indication: prepubertal cryptorchidism not due to anatomic obstruction. The indication attestation includes absence of anatomic obstruction; clinical evidence requires manual review.",
    "Patient must be male. Either sex=male or patient_male=true supplies the approval fact; an explicitly negative supplied fact causes denial. Infertility and any off-label indication, including weight loss, are denied.",
    "HCG may induce testicular descent when descent would have occurred at puberty and may help predict whether orchiopexy will be needed. Response is usually temporary, though sometimes permanent.",
    "No authorization duration or quantity limit is specified in the source PDF. Remains partial; clinical attestations require verification. PDL status unknown."
  ],
